The '''Poker Hall of Fame''' is the [[hall of fame]] of professional [[poker]] in the United States. Founded in [[Las Vegas Valley|Las Vegas]], it was created in 1979 by [[Benny Binion]], the owner of the [[Horseshoe Casino]], to preserve the names and legacies of the world's greatest poker players and to serve as a tourist attraction to his casino.<ref name = "tourism">{{cite web|url=http://www.pokernews.com/wsop/hall-of-fame/|title=Poker Hall of Fame|access-date=June 20, 2009|publisher=Poker News}}</ref>

Binion was known for the creative ways in which he marketed his casino. In 1949, he convinced [[Johnny Moss]] and [[Nick Dandolos|Nick "The Greek" Dandolos]] to play high-stakes poker [[heads up poker|heads up]] where the public could watch them.<ref name = "MrMoss" /> In 1970, he invited a group of poker players to compete in what would be the first [[World Series of Poker]] (WSOP). When Harrah's Entertainment, later known as [[Caesars Entertainment Corporation|Caesars Entertainment]], acquired the rights to the WSOP in 2004, it also assumed ownership of the Poker Hall of Fame.<ref name ="WSOP History" />  Currently, membership in the Poker Hall of Fame is handled directly by the WSOP.<ref name = "WSOPHall">{{cite web|url=http://www.wsop.com/pokerhalloffame/index.asp|title=WSOP Poker Hall of Fame|access-date=November 3, 2011|publisher=World Series of Poker}}</ref>

As of 2026, 64 people have been inducted into the Poker Hall of Fame, 33 of whom are still living.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokernewsreport.com/poker-hall-of-fame-stats-and-facts-5501|title=Poker Hall of Fame Stats and Facts|date=October 30, 2011|publisher=Poker News Report|access-date=December 5, 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.espn.com/poker/story/_/id/8525208/eric-drache-brian-sailor-roberts-inducted-poker-hall-fame |title=Drache and Roberts to enter HOF |first=Andrew |last=Feldman |work=[[ESPN.com]] |date=October 19, 2012 |access-date=October 21, 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.wsop.com/news/jason-koon-inducted-into-the-poker-hall-of-fame/|title=Jason Koon Inducted into the Poker Hall of Fame|publisher=World Series of Poker|date=August 2026|access-date=August 7, 2026}}</ref>

In July 2023, an exhibit devoted to the Poker Hall of Fame opened in the Horseshoe Las Vegas, owned by Caesar’s Entertainment. The exhibit acknowledges poker’s most legendary players with a Gallery of Champions, WSOP bracelets and rings.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Holden |first=Dominic  |date=July 14, 2024 |title=PATRIK ANTONIUS ANNOUNCED AS 2024 POKER HALL OF FAME INDUCTEE |url=https://www.wsop.com/news/2024/Jul/14023/PATRIK-ANTONIUS-ANNOUNCED-AS-2024--POKER-HALL-OF-FAME-INDUCTEE.html |access-date=July 14, 2024 |publisher=WSOP.com}}</ref>

== Requirements ==
Before the 2009 World Series of Poker, then-WSOP Commissioner [[Jeffrey Pollack]] announced that the process for becoming a member into the Poker Hall of Fame would undergo a slight modification. Starting in 2009, the Poker Hall of Fame started accepting nominations from the public.  This move was intended to increase interest in the Hall. Almost immediately after this decision was announced, [[Party Poker]] started an online campaign to get its representative and [[World Poker Tour]] commentator [[Mike Sexton]] elected to the Hall.<ref name= "Mike">{{cite web|url=http://www.cardplayer.com/poker-news/6828-nomination-process-for-the-poker-hall-of-fame-open|title=Nomination Process for the Poker Hall of Fame Open|last=Murphy|first=Stephen|date=May 29, 2009|access-date=June 13, 2009|publisher=CardPlayer Magazine}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tightpoker.com/news/mike-sexton-deserves-place-in-pokers-hall-of-fame-1074/|title=Mike Sexton Deserves Place In Poker's Hall of Fame|date=May 27, 2009|access-date=June 13, 2009|last=Zusman|first=Joe|work=Tight Poker |publisher=PartyPoker}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokerpages.com/poker-news/news/partypoker-pushes-for-mike-sextons-induction-to-poker-hall-of-fame-31685.htm|title=PartyPoker Pushes for Mike Sexton's Induction to Poker Hall of Fame|date=May 28, 2009|publisher=Poker Pages|access-date=June 20, 2009|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090531081331/http://www.pokerpages.com/poker-news/news/partypoker-pushes-for-mike-sextons-induction-to-poker-hall-of-fame-31685.htm|archive-date=May 31, 2009}}</ref>  Other poker sites, namely [[PokerStars]]' [[Tom McEvoy]], followed suit by pushing their own poker professionals.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokernewsdaily.com/pokerstars-pushes-tom-mcevoy-for-poker-hall-of-fame-3061/|title=PokerStars Pushes Tom McEvoy for Poker Hall of Fame|last=Jenkins|first=Tom|date=June 22, 2009|access-date=August 6, 2009|publisher=PokerDailyNews}}</ref>  The requirements for the Poker Hall of Fame are as follows:
*''A gambler must have played poker against acknowledged top competition,''
*''Played for high stakes,''
*''Played consistently well, gained the respect of peers,''
*''And stood the test of time.''
*''Or, for non-players, contributed to the overall growth and success of the game of poker, with indelible positive and lasting results.''<ref name ="WSOP History">{{cite web|url=http://www.worldseriesofpoker.com/pokerhalloffame/index.asp|title=A Brief History of the Poker Hall of Fame|publisher=Harrah's Entertainment|access-date=June 13, 2009}}</ref><ref name = "shapiro">{{cite web|url=http://www.cardplayer.com/magazine/article/16937|title=Barbara and the Poker Hall of Fame|date=August 15, 2007|access-date=March 3, 2008|last=Shapiro|first=Max|publisher=CardPlayer Magazine}}</ref>

In 2009, 23-year-old online poker professional [[Tom Dwan]] was a finalist for the Poker Hall of Fame because of public balloting. As a result, a new age requirement was added in 2011. This rule, known as the "Chip Reese Rule", established a minimum age of 40 to be inducted into the Hall of Fame. This new requirement eliminated some players who were regular nominees over the previous years, such as [[Phil Ivey]] and [[Daniel Negreanu]] (both of whom were eventually inducted upon reaching the age threshold).<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pocketfives.com/articles/2011-poker-hall-fame-nominations-now-open-wsop-rolls-586591/|title=2011 Poker Hall of Fame nomination now open as WSOP rolls on|author=P5 Staff|publisher=Pocket Fives|date=July 5, 2011|access-date=October 28, 2011}}</ref>

==Award==
Admission into the Poker Hall of Fame is considered one of the greatest honors in poker.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokerpages.com/articles/archives/west07.htm|title=Baxter, Cloutier Admitted to Poker Hall of Fame|publisher=Poker Pages|last=West|first=Justin|access-date=June 20, 2009|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090923182732/http://www.pokerpages.com/articles/archives/west07.htm|archive-date=September 23, 2009}}</ref> In his acceptance speech, [[T. J. Cloutier]] declared, "It's one of two things I've always wanted to win."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokerlistings.com/player-interviews/the-press-conference-part-1-this-years-poker-hall-of-famers|title=The Press Conference Part 1: This Year's Poker Hall of Famers|publisher=Poker Listing|date = August 1, 2006|access-date=March 3, 2008}}</ref>  [[Barbara Enright]], the first woman inducted into the Hall, considers her induction to be a "lifetime achievement honor."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://pokerworks.com/poker-news/2007/07/05/hellmuth-enright-join-poker-hall-of-fame.html|title=Hellmuth, Enright join Poker Hall of Fame|last=Tuscaloosa |first=Johnny|date=May 27, 2007|access-date=March 3, 2008|publisher= Poker Works}}</ref>

Before being acquired by Harrah's Casino, [[R.S. Owens & Company]] was commissioned to design an award for Poker Hall of Famers.  The award was an eight-inch-tall piece of glass with a hand of cards sandblasted at the bottom, the winner's name, and the words "Poker Hall of Fame" in a circle. The circle had a gold emblem bonded to the glass and had the Binion's Horseshoe Casino logo in it. There was a gold plated base with three gold-plated stacks of chips.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.rsowens.com/galleries/custom/product.asp?ITEM_ID=2013|archive-url=https://archive.today/20120910110844/http://www.rsowens.com/galleries/custom/product.asp?ITEM_ID=2013|url-status=dead|archive-date=September 10, 2012|title=Poker Hall of Fame Custom Award|publisher=R.S. Owens|access-date=March 3, 2008}}</ref>

